<title>FRANCE: LVMH, Guinness, Grand Met meeting ends.</title>
<headline>LVMH, Guinness, Grand Met meeting ends.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The chairmen of LVMH, Guinness and Grand Met concluded a one-hour meeting at LVMH's Paris headquarters on Wednesday but did not make any announcement, a source close to the talks said.</p>
<p>&quot;The meeting is over. It lasted one hour,&quot; the source said.</p>
<p>The three chairmen met to discuss their differences over the planned merger of Guinness and Grand Met.</p>
<p>LVMH, the biggest shareholder in both the British companies, opposes their merger plan as it stands and wants to bring together the three companies' drinks businesses. LVMH officials were not immediately available for comment when contacted.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
